# libomp is not built with ThreadSanitizer, so its internal allocator
# (__kmp_allocate and __kmp_free recycling per-thread team and task blocks)
# and its own mutex bookkeeping read as races. libarcher annotates the
# OpenMP happens-before edges around user code; it cannot annotate the
# runtime private state.
#
# This is narrow on purpose. Every access it suppresses is inside libomp:
# a full-suite run on 2026-08-26 reported 3,626 races, and all 7,252 racing
# accesses sat at five libomp offsets with no bonsai frame among them.
# Anything in bonsai code still fails the build.
called_from_lib:libomp.so
